<title>RUSSIA: Aeroflot starts Moscow-Bishkek service.</title>
<headline>Aeroflot starts Moscow-Bishkek service.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's international carrier Aeroflot will start regular passenger flights between Moscow and the Kyrgyz capital Bishkek from February, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Leonid Mokhov, Aeroflot domestic and CIS department deputy chief, told Reuters that an agreement between Aeroflot and the Kyrgyz national carrier had been signed last week.</p>
<p>&quot;We will operate Tupolev-154 or Ilyushin-62 jets making one flight a week,&quot; Mokhov said, adding that eventually the number of flights could increase to three a week.</p>
<p>&quot;The Kyrgyz carrier has agreed to stop its four flights a week in Aeroflot's favour,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
